UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East might have considered playing the @HJ or a low heart at trick one hoping to cover the @HK with the @HA. But it turns out that can never be the right play. West led the @H10 which is a high heart. So West either has a doubleton heart, which means I started with Qx in hearts or a singleton heart. In either case playing the @HA is correct.|
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If West had a doubleton it doesn't matter. However, with a singleton West can get a heart ruff, as it what happened here. Counting out suits like this is crucial to playing expert defense. East/West did the best they could.|
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


