md|1SA873H42D864CQ953,SQJT95HAJT5DT5CA8,SHKQ9763DK3CK7642,SK642H8DAQJ972CJT|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|1S|mb|2H|mb|4H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|An excellent bid by East. 4@H is a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=splinters,Splinter^*N|CP||FP||at|, showing 4+ spades, singleton (or rarely void) in hearts and game forcing values.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 34 ***** |


mb|P|MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|4@S is West's best call. On the other hand, change his hand around a little, for example make the @HA the @DA. Now If that were the hand, now West knows he has no wasted values in hearts and slam is possible. So West might bid 4N instead and bid 6 with enough key cards.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|With 6-5 distribution, at favorable vulnerability (we are not vulnerable, they are) and the really important spade void North should bid 5@C, hoping to sacrifice in either hearts or clubs. North has little defense and lots of offense.|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


mb|5C|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This is what is known as a ^*BForcing Pass^*n situation. If East has a clear bid, she can make it, either double or something else. But she doesn't. So she passes.|
PG| ***** 37 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|An important bidding principle is that if you constructively bid game, meaning you bid game because you have the values to do so (as opposed to sacrificing or preempting) and the opponents bid over your game, you cannot let them play undoubled. You must either double or bid one more.|
PG| ***** 38 ***** |


mb|5H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Personally, I would have doubled but this may work out.|
PG| ***** 39 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Pass by North is correct.|
PG| ***** 40 ***** |


mb|5S|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 41 ***** |


