UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|We did our job pushing them to 5@S and it turns out to make. In 5@C we lose 2 diamonds, 1 heart, 1 heart ruff, and 1 club for down 3. So they did a little better making 5 spades. In Match Points it is less clear what to do. But in IMPs it is probably better for West to double as it is not clear at all that 5@S is making and if spades were 3-1 instead of 4-0, we would perhaps be down 4.|
PG| ***** 51 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In general, ^*BThe 5 Level Belongs to the Opponents^*n is a very good rule that most do not follow. That means, you should not bid 5 over 5 unless you have a really good reason and here you do not have a good reason.|
PG| ***** 52 ***** |


