pc|C6|pc|CJ|pc|CQ|pc|HJ|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now 4@H is cold. But the question is how to play the diamonds. I know West started with 1 heart and probably started with 5 clubs at most. If that is the case, that leaves West with 7 cards in spades and diamonds and he doesn't have 5 spades meaning he has 3 diamonds at least.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So the best way to play the diamonds is to play the @DA and finesse West for @DQ. Not to mention that if he doesn't have the @DQ he opened with 9 HCP.|
